 ### Stable Linear Raymarching
-A raymarching loop that uses stable, uniform linear marching between bounding bounds to eliminate artifacts like spots, missing clouds, noise, and banding, replacing unstable backing-up/bifurcated stepping loops [S2, unofficial]. It corrects empty space skipping using a robust positive-step bifurcated step size logic to handle coordinate jumping and infinite loops [S2, unofficial]. Choose this when rendering low-resolution volumes where unstable stepping causes visible artifacts [S2, unofficial]. It is a variant focused on stability in low-resolution contexts, whereas Oversampled 3D Ray March focuses on LOD tiling correctness [S1, unofficial].
